  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday) \nIssued at 249 PM CDT Sat May 9 2026\n\nA dry and stable pattern will prevail for most of next week.\nCooler temperatures are expected on Monday in the wake of the cold\nfront on Sunday. Highs will be in the upper 70s and lower 80s,\nwith overnight lows in the 50s. Otherwise, an upper level ridge\nover the southwestern U.S. will migrate eastward into our area by\nthe middle of the week. The center of the ridge axis will shift to\nthe east of the region on Thursday and Friday with generally zonal\nflow aloft prevailing into next weekend. Thus, rain chances will \nremain low through Saturday. Temperatures will warm into the upper\n80s to mid 90s across most of the area from Wednesday into next \nweekend, with some upper 90s possible in the Big County.",
